+ * needs no interpretation at all: PLL_EN is ALREADY 0 on that running board
+ * (PLL_NPU_CTRL = 0x01105300), so nothing on it can be running off this PLL.
+ * What clk_disable_unused() does here is write 0 to a bit that is already 0.
+ *
+ * The name "npupll" is the UM's, not ours: NPU_CLK's mux prints its source 000
+ * as "NPUPLL". Calling the tap "npu-pll" beside a VCO called
+ * "pll-npu" would differ by word order alone in a clk_summary dump.
+ *
+ * VCO WINDOW. Table 4-2's PLL_NPU row reads 1.26G~2.52G, M1 1/2, P0 1~8
+ * (A733 user manual) -- the same window as PLL_DE and the video PLLs, so the
+ * same floor applies for the same reason, and it is 1272 rather than 1260:
+ * ccu_nm_determine_rate() clamps a too-low request to min_rate while
+ * ccu_nm_set_rate() does not clamp at all, so a min_rate of 1260 MHz would be
+ * agreed on and then programmed as 24 x 52 = 1248 MHz, under the documented
+ * window. 1272 = 24 x 53 and 2520 = 24 x 105 are both exact from the 24 MHz
+ * reference. ⚠ Table 4-2 also prints PLL_NPU's TYPICAL VCO as 1.8G while the
+ * typical-configuration table and the register default both say 1680 MHz;
+ * that split hits five rows of that table and is a defect in one of the two,
+ * which the UM never resolves. It changes nothing here -- both numbers are
+ * inside the window and this driver programs neither by hand.
+ *
+ * ⚠ A523 PROVENANCE, AND IT IS THE DANGEROUS KIND: ccu-sun55i-a523.c DOES
+ * model an NPU, in a shape that looks exactly like what is wanted here. Its
+ * OFFSETS, its enable bit, its tap topology and its parent set are all wrong
+ * for this part -- and the offsets are the expensive half: neither 0x080 nor
+ * 0x6E0 appears in the CCU register list of the A733 user manual, so a
+ * carried-over model would write into an undocumented hole and leave the
+ * block dark while every write looked like it had succeeded.
+ *
+ * ⚠ It is NOT true that every number in it is wrong, and an earlier draft of
+ * this comment said so. .lock = BIT(28) is identical and correct on both
+ * parts; the N field geometry is (shift 8, width 8, offset 1) on both; .m is
+ * byte-identical; and the module clock's M [4:0] / mux [26:24] widths agree.
+ * An overclaim in the section whose job is to catch A523 numbers is worse
+ * than no section, so here is the list that is actually true:
+ *
+ *   A523 (ccu-sun55i-a523.c)          A733 (UM 4.1.6, and this file)
+ *   PLL_NPU reg 0x080  (:319)         PLL_NPU_CTRL_REG 0x02A0
+ *   .enable = BIT(27)  (:321)         PLL_EN is BIT(31); on the A733 bit 27
+ *                                     is PLL_OUTPUT_GATE, so the inherited
+ *                                     model would toggle the output gate,
+ *                                     never enable the PLL, and still report
+ *                                     a rate from the register fields
+ *   _SUNXI_CCU_MULT_MIN(8, 8, 11)     N >= 12 and N <= 255 here.
+ *                       (:323)        ⚠ NOT an offset difference -- an earlier
+ *                                     draft claimed the A523 reads N as the
+ *                                     raw field. It does not:
+ *                                     _SUNXI_CCU_MULT_MIN expands with offset
+ *                                     1 (ccu_mult.h:26), so both parts compute
+ *                                     N = field + 1. What differs is the
+ *                                     BOUNDS: its min 11 admits field 10, one
+ *                                     step below the UM's minimum of 11 for
+ *                                     the PLL_N field value (a bound on
+ *                                     the FIELD), and its max 0 becomes
+ *                                     1 << width = 256 in ccu_nm.c, one above
+ *                                     the UM's field range 0..254
+ *   TWO fixed-factor taps, /2 and     ONE tap, and it is PROGRAMMABLE:
+ *     /4 (:332, :335), hung off the   PLL_OUTPUT_DIV [22:20], P0 = field + 1,
+ *     ccu_nm itself as "4x"           1..8
+ *   CLK_SET_RATE_GATE  (:329)         CLK_SET_RATE_UNGATE -- see the lock
+ *                                     sequence, which needs the PLL ON while
+ *                                     ccu_nm_set_rate() polls
+ *   npu module clock at 0x6e0 (:496)  NPU_CLK_REG 0x0B00
+ *   4 parents: PERI0_480M, 600M,      7 parents: NPUPLL, PERI0_800M, 600M,
+ *     800M, PLL_NPU_2X  (:490-495)    480M, VE0PLL, VE1PLL, DEPLL3X --
+ *                                     different set AND different order, so
+ *                                     even the three shared parents sit at
+ *                                     different indices
+ *   no NPU reset in its reset header  three, NPU_BGR bits 16/17/18
+ *   no NPU bus gate, no matrix gates  NPU_BGR bit 0, AHB_MAT bit 6,
+ *                                     MBUS_MAT bit 18
+ *
+ * The only thing carried across is the divider/mux WIDTHS of the module clock
+ * (M [4:0], mux [26:24]) -- and they were re-read in the A733
+ * user manual rather than taken, because a width that happens to
+ * agree is still not evidence.
+ */
