+ * DIAGNOSTIC. Say so plainly, because the obvious guess -- "it just shows as
+ * an orphan in clk_summary" -- is wrong and was written here first.
+ * clk_core_get_parent_by_index() returns NULL, so the clock is parentless; and
+ * CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT sends ccu_mux_helper_determine_rate() down the
+ * branch that does best_parent = clk_hw_get_parent(hw) followed by
+ * clk_hw_get_rate(best_parent) (ccu_mux.c) -- and clk_hw_get_rate() reads
+ * hw->core with no NULL check, unlike clk_core_get_rate_nolock() which has
+ * one. So the first clk_set_rate()/clk_round_rate() on such a clock
+ * dereferences NULL. The same is true of encoding 111, which the UM does not
+ * document at all: the field is 3 bits, this array is 7 long, and
+ * ccu_mux_helper_get_parent() hands the raw value back.
+ *
+ * What forecloses it is in the device tree, and that makes `arm64-dts-a733-add-the-npu`'s
+ * assigned-clock-parents load-bearing rather than decorative:
+ * of_clk_set_defaults() runs from platform_probe() BEFORE drv->probe()
