+ * consumer's first rate request can ever be made. On silicon the field has
+ * never been anything but 000 anyway -- which is also its reset value.
+ *
+ * The readings behind that: NPU_CLK = 0x00000000 on the 6 GiB board idle, 0x80000000 on
+ * the 6 GiB board with mainline etnaviv resumed, and 0x00000000 on a board on the vendor kernel under
+ * the vendor 6.6 vipcore -- CLK_SRC_SEL = 000 in every one, across two
+ * unrelated driver stacks.
+ *
+ *
+ * CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT | CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT is the pair `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-video-plls-and-edp-tv-pixel-clock` and `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-display-engine-clock-gate-reset`
+ * give the display clocks, for the same two reasons. Propagation, so one
+ * clk_set_rate() configures the chain instead of a driver poking CCU
+ * registers behind the framework. NO_REPARENT, because which source drives
+ * the NPU is a pipeline decision that belongs in the device tree -- and
+ * without it ccu_mux_helper_determine_rate() would walk all seven parents on
+ * every rate request, including the two that resolve to nothing.
+ *
+ * ⚠ Index 110 is DEPLL3X, and `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-display-engine-clock-gate-reset`'s header carries a standing warning about
+ * it: "a future VE, NPU or DRAM driver that selects DEPLL3X from its own mux
+ * inherits a clock the display retunes". This driver does not select it. The
+ * device tree pins index 000, NO_REPARENT keeps the framework from wandering
+ * there, and the slot is modelled only so a register found at 110 is
+ * described correctly rather than silently mis-named.
